# Repository instance names

A variable, field, or parameter that holds a repository ends in `Repo`. The name without that suffix is the data it returns.

Type names stay as they are (`ReadonlyRepository`, `CRUDRepository`). The suffix is on the instance.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — users is both the repository and the rows
var users = new ReadonlyRepository<User>(connection);
await foreach (var user in users.Read()) { }

// ✅ GOOD
var usersRepo = new ReadonlyRepository<User>(connection);
await foreach (var user in usersRepo.Read()) { }
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const users = new ReadonlyRepository(User, connection);

// ✅ GOOD
const usersRepo = new ReadonlyRepository(User, connection);
```

```rust
// ❌ BAD
let users = ReadonlyRepository::new(connection)?;

// ✅ GOOD
let users_repo = ReadonlyRepository::new(connection)?;
```
